{
  "_about": "Where each scene's subject sits, as an x centre in the 1536-pixel-wide header. derive.py cuts every derived crop around it. wide = the 2:1 social and 1.9:1 OG crops; phone = the 4:3 phone hero. Picked by eye on 2026-11-06 so Ouro and the product both stay in frame. Phone centres moved on 2026-11-06 so Ouro stands whole, tail and all, with about 96 px of scene to his right (measured from his green extent in each header); several canonical crops had him touching or past the right edge. phoneAspect (optional, default [4, 3]) widens the phone crop for a scene whose characters stand too far apart for 4:3; sites size the phone hero from the file's own width and height. A night scene (<scene>-dark) is cut with its day twin's centres; it gets its own entry only where its drawing sits differently. og (optional) moves the narrower 1.9:1 OG crop's centre on its own, where the 2:1 centre would cut a figure. wideFit \"whole\" (optional) makes the social and OG cards from the whole header under its real sky (brand/skies/<scene>.webp, from the master or an outpaint), cut to the card from the foot up, for a scene whose cast is wider than either card (render QA, 2026-11-14: these crops cut Ouro or a person at the edge).",
